---
const beforeCode = `---
name: pdf-processor
description: 'Process PDF files for various tasks'
---`;

const afterCode = `---
name: pdf-processor
description: "Extract PDF text, rotate pages, and merge existing PDFs. WHEN: \\"extract PDF text\\", \\"rotate PDF pages\\", \\"merge PDFs\\"."
---`;
---

<section class="py-24 md:py-32 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-light-gray">
      Before &amp; After
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mid-gray text-lg max-w-2xl">
      From vague to precise. Both examples can satisfy the portable format;
      the improvement is clearer scope, not mandatory negative routing syntax.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-16 grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-mid-gray">Before</span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-mid-gray/60">Low</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="bg-dark-gray p-6 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto"><code class="block text-mid-gray"><span class="text-orange-accent/60">---</span>
<span class="text-orange-accent">name:</span> <span class="text-light-gray">pdf-processor</span>
<span class="text-orange-accent">description:</span> <span class="text-light-gray">'Process PDF files for various tasks'</span>
<span class="text-orange-accent/60">---</span></code></pre>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-light-gray">After</span>
          <span class="text-xs font-mono text-orange-accent">Medium-High</span>
        </div>
        <pre class="bg-dark-gray p-6 font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed overflow-x-auto"><code class="block text-light-gray">{afterCode}</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
